---

Why this license? (not legal advice)

We follow the source-available, open-core model used by Elastic (Elastic License 2.0),
n8n (Sustainable Use License), Confluent (Community License) and others:
- The framework, integrations, portal and SDKs are source-available
- The compiled kernels and engine remain proprietary, and their usage limits are enforced in the
  binaries themselves
- Community builders get full access to build on top of Algenta
- Commercial deployment beyond the thresholds requires a paid license

